---
/**
 * PROTOTYPE V4 "One stack, two grounds": a single section drawing. The app and the records are drawn
 * once; only the ground under them splits into your servers or our hosting. Notes on the right, joined by
 * leader lines, say what each layer means.
 */
---
<figure class="o4">
  <div class="o4-row">
    <div class="own-layer own-layer--app">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 3h12v10H2z M2 6h12" /><circle cx="4" cy="4.5" r=".6" /><circle cx="5.8" cy="4.5" r=".6" /></svg>
      <span>noma</span><span class="own-tag">MIT</span>
    </div>
    <p class="o4-note"><b>Same code</b>Line for line, wherever it runs.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="o4-row">
    <div class="own-layer own-layer--data">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="8" cy="3.5" rx="5.5" ry="2" /><path d="M2.5 3.5v9c0 1.1 2.5 2 5.5 2s5.5-.9 5.5-2v-9 M2.5 8c0 1.1 2.5 2 5.5 2s5.5-.9 5.5-2" /></svg>
      <span>Your records</span><span class="own-tag">PostgreSQL</span>
    </div>
    <p class="o4-note"><b>Yours</b>In a standard database you can read without noma.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="o4-row o4-row--ground">
    <div class="o4-ground">
      <p><span>Your servers</span><span class="own-who">You run it</span></p>
      <span class="o4-or">or</span>
      <p><span>Our hosting</span><span class="own-who">We run it for you</span></p>
    </div>
    <p class="o4-note"><b>Your choice</b>Pick one now, switch later.</p>
  </div>
</figure>
